  "guidebook": {
    "intro": "Swahili coast cooking mixes African, Arab and Indian kitchens. Follow a recipe for pilau, and learn the words a cook shouts across the kitchen.",
    "phrases": [
      { "target": "Weka sufuria motoni.", "base": "Put the pot on the fire." },
      { "target": "Kata kitunguu.", "base": "Cut the onion." },
      { "target": "Ongeza chumvi kidogo.", "base": "Add a little salt." },
      { "target": "Changanya pamoja.", "base": "Mix together." },
      { "target": "Leo tunapika pilau.", "base": "Today we’re cooking pilau." },
      { "target": "Karibu chakula!", "base": "Come and eat!" }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "ni-place",
        "title": "-ni: in, on, at",
        "body": [
          "Add **-ni** to a noun to mean “in”, “on” or “at” it: **moto** (fire) → **motoni** (on the fire), **soko** → **sokoni** (at the market), **shule** → **shuleni** (at school).",
          "You’ve been using it since **jikoni** (in the kitchen) and **nyumbani** (at home)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "kitchen-verbs",
        "title": "Recipe verbs",
        "body": [
          "Recipes are a string of commands: **Kata**, **kaanga**, **ongeza**, **changanya**. To two or more cooks, add **-ni**: **Kateni vitunguu!**",
          "**-sha** often means “make it do”: **chemka** (boil, by itself) gives **chemsha** (bring to the boil), **safi** (clean) gives **safisha** (make clean)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Rice has three names",
        "body": [
          "Rice growing in the field is **mpunga**, uncooked grains are **mchele**, and cooked rice is **wali**. Spiced with meat it becomes **pilau**, the dish for weddings and Eid."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Come and eat",
        "body": [
          "If you arrive while people are eating, you will hear **Karibu chakula!** It’s a real invitation. Saying **Asante, nimeshiba** (thanks, I’m full) is a polite way to decline."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "sw-pilau-lesson",
      "title": "A pilau lesson",
      "unlockAfter": "u24s3l1",
      "cast": ["baraka", "emma"],
      "summary": "Baraka teaches Emma to cook pilau at his stall in Mombasa.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "baraka", "target": "Emma, leo nitakufundisha kupika pilau.", "base": "Emma, today I’ll teach you to cook pilau." },
          "gloss": { "nitakufundisha": "I will teach you" }
        },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Safi! Kwanza nifanye nini?", "base": "Great! What should I do first?" },
          "gloss": { "nifanye": "should I do" }
        },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "baraka", "target": "Kata vitunguu, halafu kaanga kwa mafuta.", "base": "Cut the onions, then fry them in oil." }
        },
        { "question": "What does Emma do first?", "options": ["Cut the onions", "Boil water", "Add salt"], "answer": 0 },
        { "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Sawa. Na viungo?", "base": "Okay. And the spices?" }, "gloss": { "viungo": "spices" } },
        {
          "line": {
            "speaker": "baraka",
            "target": "Ongeza bizari ya pilau, nyama na mchele. Halafu maji.",
            "base": "Add the pilau spices, meat and rice. Then water."
          },
          "gloss": { "bizari ya pilau": "pilau spice mix", "mchele": "uncooked rice" }
        },
        { "question": "What goes in with the spices?", "options": ["Meat and rice", "Sugar", "Milk"], "answer": 0 },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Inanukia vizuri sana!", "base": "It smells really good!" },
          "gloss": { "Inanukia": "it smells" }
        },
        {
          "line": {
            "speaker": "baraka",
            "target": "Karibu chakula! Pilau yako ni tamu kuliko yangu!",
            "base": "Come and eat! Your pilau is tastier than mine!"
          },
          "gloss": { "kuliko": "than" }
        },
        {
          "question": "How does Baraka say “come and eat”?",
          "options": ["Karibu chakula", "Kata vitunguu", "Ongeza chumvi"],
          "answer": 0,
          "optionsLang": "target"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
